/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 77 0 R
/T (Theory : A distributed chat application enables multiple clients to communicate over a network using a central server. The server utilizes TCP sockets to maintain reliable, bi-directional connections with each client. Multithreading is employed to handle concurrent client connections, enabling real-time message broadcasting across the network. A graphical user interface \(GUI\) built using Java Swing provides a seamless and interactive user experience. )
/E (Theory : A distributed chat application enables multiple clients to communicate over a network using a central server. The server utilizes TCP sockets to maintain reliable, bi-directional connections with each client. Multithreading is employed to handle concurrent client connections, enabling real-time message broadcasting across the network. A graphical user interface \(GUI\) built using Java Swing provides a seamless and interactive user experience. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
