947 0 obj
<<
/Title (Theory: Socket options in Java allow developers to fine-tune the behavior of the underlying network protocols \(like TCP\) to optimize performance, handle edge cases, or adjust latency. SO_KEEPALIVE ensures inactive connections are checked periodically. SO_LINGER specifies how long to wait before forcefully closing a socket if un-sent data remains. SO_SNDBUF and SO_RCVBUF set hints for the size of the underlying network I/O buffers. Finally, TCP_NODELAY disables Nagle's algorithm, forcing packets to be sent immediately rather than waiting to fill a buffer, which is crucial for time-sensitive or low-latency applications.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 602 0 R
/Prev 841 0 R
/Next 842 0 R
>>
endobj
