/Title (Theory: A day-time server provides the current date and time to any client that connects to it. In a concurrent implementation, the server is capable of handling multiple client requests simultaneously by creating a new thread for each incoming TCP connection. This ensures that the server remains responsive and does not block while servicing a particular client, demonstrating effective use of Java Socket programming and multithreading.)
